cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pydyn, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pydyn: a serial Python reference of the TM5 dynamic core"
abstract: >-
  A NumPy transcription of the transport core of the TM5 atmospheric chemistry-transport
  model that is bitwise equal to the production Fortran under stated conditions (no FMA
  contraction; the model's own FFT, LAPACK and libm), with the tests that prove it.
authors:
  - family-names: Pera
    given-names: Ash
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9019-279X"
    affiliation: "CIRES, University of Colorado Boulder; NOAA Global Monitoring Laboratory"
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23974450
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/pera-noaa/pydyn"
keywords:
  - TM5
  - atmospheric transport
  - reference implementation
  - bitwise reproducibility
references:
